WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:05.400
Anyone who holds more than just a passing
knowledge of the SCP Foundation has likely

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.970
heard the name of one Doctor Jack Bright.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:13.400
Like a lot of the other high-ranking research
staff, his name carries with it a reputation

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.260
for anomalous expertise far beyond many working
at the Foundation.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:22.410
Having risen through the ranks and achieved
the position of Personnel Director for Sites

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:29.679
17, 19, and 63, Doctor Bright may just seem
like a highly competent and devoted member

00:00:29.679 --> 00:00:31.500
of the organization.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:37.040
But the history of the man himself is one
that will be forever linked with tragedy and

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.230
trauma.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:43.390
Jack Bright’s life has been turbulent, to
say the least, with themes of rebirth and

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:49.200
regeneration constantly following him and
his family… and all the curses that those

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.230
ideas bring.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:56.710
Born to Adam and Evelyn Bright, young Jack
has sadly never experienced what many would

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:58.699
consider an ‘ordinary’ life.

00:00:58.699 --> 00:01:05.410
You see, both his parents were also researchers
within the SCP Foundation, meaning that since

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:10.530
birth, Jack Bright has never known a life
that wasn’t linked with the Foundation and

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.450
its many anomalous happenings.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:15.280
And it didn’t stop there either.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:19.851
At some point, Doctor Adam Bright would rise
through the ranks of the Foundation, much

00:01:19.851 --> 00:01:22.450
like his son would later come to do.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:27.880
Adam progressed from researcher to personnel
director to site director and then eventually

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:32.049
even to the high station of O5 Council member.

00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:36.439
But this career trajectory within the Foundation
was cut short when Jack Bright’s father

00:01:36.439 --> 00:01:42.790
met an untimely end, assassinated on the orders
of his fellow O5 Council members.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:43.790
But why?

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:48.659
What could have led to young Jack suffering
the loss of his Foundation employed father?

00:01:48.659 --> 00:01:51.330
Well, it had to do with the other Bright children.

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:57.789
You see, Jack was far from an only child;
in fact, he had a considerable number of siblings.

00:01:57.789 --> 00:02:03.000
While you might be forgiven for thinking this
would provide a younger Jack Bright with equals,

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.670
friends that he would at least endure his
anomalous adjacent childhood with, this was

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.929
sadly not the case.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:15.030
One of Jack’s brothers, TJ Bright, was born
with his very own anomalous abilities.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:20.870
TJ had something of a gift for healing, possessing
the power to absorb the injuries and illnesses

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:25.010
of anyone around him, purely through physical
touch.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:30.250
But the unfortunate side effect is that TJ
also takes on another person’s ailments

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:35.129
himself, experiencing their pain and sickness,
so they don’t have to.

00:02:35.129 --> 00:02:39.340
If you’re Jack Bright, it had to have been
hard to see your younger brother suffering

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:43.590
from wounds and diseases passed onto him so
that others don’t suffer.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:49.530
But there’s still the lingering question:
what happened to jack and TJ’s father, Adam?

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:54.890
What led to his assassination, and what role
did TJ play in the events leading up to that

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:56.390
untimely death?

00:02:56.390 --> 00:03:01.489
Well, like much of Doctor Bright’s family
life, it began with a tragedy.

00:03:01.489 --> 00:03:06.810
Trying for another baby, Adam and Evelyn eventually
had a new daughter, giving Jack, TJ, and their

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.980
other siblings a new sister.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:15.080
However, this was sadly short-lived, as the
newest member of the Bright family was stillborn.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:19.530
Bearing witness to the grief that would have
caused his parents was no doubt hard on Jack.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:22.580
But even more upsetting was what came next.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:28.110
Naturally, having both studied anomalies within
the SCP Foundation, Evelyn and Adam were willing

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:32.569
to defy death itself in order to get their
newly born daughter back.

00:03:32.569 --> 00:03:38.150
And luckily for them, they had been presented
with the perfect anomaly to achieve this goal,

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:42.910
in the form of their young son TJ and his
regenerative powers.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:48.319
However, what resulted, was a creature that
later became known as SCP-321.

00:03:48.319 --> 00:03:54.400
While TJ was able to revive the child, her
body aged at a rapidly accelerated rate.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:59.120
She became devoid of melanin in her hair,
eyes, and skin.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:05.840
Still able to vocalize but unable to intelligibly
speak, SCP-321 is known to have spatial awareness

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:09.319
issues, as well as a low level of intelligence.

00:04:09.319 --> 00:04:14.650
On top of that, SCP-321 seemed to have inherited
some of her brother TJ Bright’s healing

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:20.850
abilities, capable of regenerating any injury
she suffers at five times the normal speed,

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:23.640
attributed to an overproduction of stem cells.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:30.320
It was this that also caused her body to rapidly
age and grow, with no signs of stopping.

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:35.600
Taken in by the SCP Foundation and given a
designation – along with TJ, who became

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:42.100
known as SCP-590 – SCP-321 was separated
from the rest of the Bright family.

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:46.630
Adam, still a Junior Researcher at the time,
pleaded with his Foundation superiors for

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:50.190
his daughter to be released back into the
care of her family.

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:52.960
Every time he made the request, it was denied.

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:57.789
It didn’t seem to matter how much higher
up the managerial ladder of the SCP Foundation

00:04:57.789 --> 00:05:03.700
Adam Bright climbed, there always seemed to
be a message from above telling him ‘no’.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:06.620
In time, he was appointed to the O5 Council.

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:12.190
It was then that Adam Bright issued a mandate
for SCP-321’s immediate release… and the

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:15.500
rest of the Council didn’t take kindly to
that.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:20.160
Trying to get his daughter back cost Adam
his life, and meant that young Jack Bright

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:25.290
had lost not only one of his brothers and
a sister, but his father too.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:31.280
Jack Bright assisted the SCP Foundation with
keeping his brother TJ, or SCP-590, contained

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:33.000
for his own safety.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.340
Unlike his remaining siblings, Jack still
seemed eager to follow in the footsteps of

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:38.930
his mom and dad.

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:43.680
Another of his sisters, Claire Pierce, was
angered by the Foundation’s actions and

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:46.180
how they had treated her family.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:50.280
This caused her to join up with the Serpent’s
Hand, a Group of interest with the goal of

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:54.370
one day exposing the SCP Foundation to the
world.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:58.600
Then there was Mikell Bright, who had the
opposite reaction to his sister.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:03.370
He devoted himself to the Foundation, becoming
one of their most skilled and highly efficient

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:07.090
field operatives, known to some as Agent Cowboy.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:11.660
Needless to say, there remains plenty of division
between the Bright siblings, something that

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:17.990
would undoubtedly exact a heavy toll on Jack,
who, for his part, continued his family’s

00:06:17.990 --> 00:06:21.819
legacy by joining the Foundation as a Junior
Researcher.

00:06:21.819 --> 00:06:26.030
This is where his life would once again be
altered forever…

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:31.569
To begin with, Jack seemed to have it easier
than most starting out at the SCP Foundation.

00:06:31.569 --> 00:06:36.590
As previously mentioned, the Bright name already
carried significant pull within the organization,

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:40.760
not only allowing him to get his foot through
the proverbial door, but also giving Jack

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:44.570
a much-needed win after his past family troubles.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:48.780
After all, he had a considerable amount of
emotional baggage and trauma to deal with,

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:53.770
so the up-and-coming Junior Researcher perhaps
deserved to coast by for a while.

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:59.090
Although it wouldn’t last long, and Jack
Bright would be irreversibly and irreparably

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:01.890
changed on one fateful day.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:07.510
It was a seemingly menial task, a job that
could have been done by anyone else, and things

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:10.110
might have turned out completely different
if they had.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:15.560
But yet, in giving it to a certain Junior
Researcher who was in good standing, the Foundation

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:18.669
completely reoriented the trajectory of Jack’s
life.

00:07:18.669 --> 00:07:25.190
He had been assigned to perform research on
SCP-963, an ornate and rather beautiful amulet

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:28.030
of unknown origin and purpose.

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:32.910
The piece was constructed from elegant white
gold, sporting an oval cut ruby surrounded

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:37.319
by thirteen brilliant cut diamonds in a starburst
pattern.

00:07:37.319 --> 00:07:41.100
It was a truly exquisite and well-crafted
piece of jewelry…

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.660
with a rather strange property to it.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:47.940
Not yet realizing the active anomalous effects
of the amulet, Doctor Bright made the honest

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:52.159
mistake of touching SCP-963 with his bare
hands.

00:07:52.159 --> 00:07:57.500
It was purely an act of human error, avoidable
and yet carrying consequences that would last

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.780
a lifetime… or several.

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:05.060
You see, as it so happened, the exact same
fateful day that Doctor Bright had made the

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:11.530
mistake of allowing SCP-963 to make contact
with his skin, another anomaly had simultaneously

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:18.889
managed to breach containment: SCP-076-2,
better known as Able.

00:08:18.889 --> 00:08:23.120
The immortal warrior tore his way through
the Foundation, pulling his bladed weaponry

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:27.810
out of a pocket dimension and cutting down
any personnel in his path as he continued

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:29.250
his rampage.

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:34.150
When the slaughter was over, the dust clearing
and Able re-contained, Junior Researcher Jack

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:37.789
Bright lay dead, tragically slain during the
breach.

00:08:37.789 --> 00:08:39.830
Or so it first seemed…

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:44.169
It was during the clean-up in the aftermath
of Able’s rampage, that a member of D Class

00:08:44.169 --> 00:08:49.070
personnel named Tom Higly, was assigned to
dispose of the bodies left in the wake of

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:51.640
the undying warrior’s massacre.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:55.880
That was when Tom unknowingly picked up the
amulet that Doctor Bright had been holding

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:57.080
when he was killed.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:09:01.899
Instantly, the D Class suffered a peculiar
change, one that would soon become a regular

00:09:01.899 --> 00:09:08.839
occurrence at the SCP Foundation: Tom Higly
became Doctor Jack Bright.

00:09:08.839 --> 00:09:13.769
Once again, like with his brother TJ’s anomalous
powers and the tragedy of his stillborn sister

00:09:13.769 --> 00:09:20.400
SCP-321, the theme of rebirth and regeneration
became a core part of Jack Bright’s life.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:24.149
He was alive once again, and inhabiting a
new body.

00:09:24.149 --> 00:09:28.529
Now, this might seem like a positive development
for the aspiring Junior Researcher.

00:09:28.529 --> 00:09:33.529
But, as Jack Bright would soon learn, the
cost of coming back from the dead was a hefty

00:09:33.529 --> 00:09:35.600
toll to pay.

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:39.520
After the Foundation had established that
the D Class now wearing the amulet was indeed

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:44.700
the person he claimed to be, they quickly
discovered that removing SCP-963 from the

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:49.300
wearer would cause all higher brain functions
to shut down immediately.

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:54.180
Replacing the amulet, the body of Tom Higly
was able to move and speak once again, albeit

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:57.500
with the voice and consciousness of Jack Bright.

00:09:57.500 --> 00:10:01.459
Through his continued experimentation with
the artifact, Doctor Bright discovered that

00:10:01.459 --> 00:10:07.670
it acted as a vessel for his consciousness,
his collected memories, and his personality.

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:13.899
They were all seemingly stored within SCP-963
and could be transferred into a new body when

00:10:13.899 --> 00:10:16.140
the amulet was worn by someone else.

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:20.810
However, part of the high cost of Jack’s
newfound immortality was the immediate loss

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:24.709
of another person for the sake of his continued
life.

00:10:24.709 --> 00:10:29.470
Placing the amulet on someone else would erase
everything about who they were, effectively

00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:33.070
killing them and wiping them clean to make
room for Jack himself.

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:37.620
It was only thanks to his mistake of being
the last person to hold the amulet, along

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:44.170
with being killed by Able directly afterwards,
that had now led to Jack being unable to die.

00:10:44.170 --> 00:10:48.260
Of course, the other large part of the cost
Jack had to pay for living forever was that

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:54.639
he essentially now had to live as a parasite,
passed on from host to host at a regular rate.

00:10:54.639 --> 00:10:59.980
He learned that, after thirty days of sustained,
continuous contact with SCP-963, Jack’s

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:03.959
consciousness could become permanently affixed
to a new body.

00:11:03.959 --> 00:11:07.950
If the amulet was removed after this occurred,
then Bright’s consciousness could still

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:13.880
be passed on to a new body, meaning he could
– in theory, at least – create multiple

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:19.380
copies of himself by transferring into new
host bodies via the amulet, and allowing them

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:23.160
to wear it for thirty days at a time to make
the change permanent.

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:29.200
Naturally, as they so often tend to do, the
SCP Foundation imposed sanctions and restrictions

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:34.480
to prevent this scenario from unfolding, executing
any hosts wearing the amulet before they could

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:37.870
reach this thirty-day permanent transfer threshold.

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:42.430
Afterwards, SCP-963 and Doctor Bright’s
consciousness would be passed on to a new

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:45.510
host, and the cycle would continue.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:50.680
However, after witnessing the immortal researcher’s
continued dedication to their cause, the Foundation

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:53.810
eventually relaxed its rules for Doctor Bright.

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:58.350
Jack then went on to continue work with the
Foundation, rising through the ranks and achieving

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:03.329
promotions to higher stations, eventually
becoming one of the most well-known researchers

00:12:03.329 --> 00:12:05.610
of SCPs to ever live.

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:10.100
But all the while, he did further examination
of SCP-963.

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:15.240
You might be fooled into thinking that immortality
would be a gift, but to Jack Bright, it’s

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:17.520
a never-ending curse.

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:23.360
Moving from host to host, only surviving because
of a simple mistake that changed his circumstances

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:28.750
in ways he could never have foreseen, Doctor
Bright lives in frustration and longs to be

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:32.660
free from what he views as a curse of eternal
life.

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:36.910
He is perpetually aware that he’ll outlive
everyone at the Foundation, have to watch

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:40.079
countless people die while he lives on.

00:12:40.079 --> 00:12:43.720
Just like he had to live on after the death
of his father.

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:48.290
This curse of immortality has led Doctor Bright
to long for a permanent death.

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:54.490
Ironically, he only became a part of SCP-963
in a moment of trying not to die, and now

00:12:54.490 --> 00:13:01.940
can’t at all, making the story of Doctor
Jack Bright a truly saddening tale.

00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:08.050
Now go and check out our “TOP 25 SAD SCPS”
compilation and “DR CLEF SCP FOUNDATION

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:11.810
RESEARCHER” for more Foundation inner-workings
and unrelenting misery!

